      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. At 1700 mg three times daily, the total is 5100 mg/day, which is about double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day in US labeling, 3000 mg/day in some other systems). For a 70 kg adult with normal renal and hepatic function, that dose risks lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the usual IR maximum)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, or another lower dose, depending on the clinical picture\n- **1700 mg twice daily with meals** (3400 mg/day), if the prescriber intends a higher total dose. This is still above the usual US maximum, so please confirm it.\n\nIf the patient is on extended-release metformin, the maximum is generally 2000 mg once daily, so the frequency would also need to change.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 5100 mg/day is intentional, please confirm that and I'll enter it as written."
      }
     ],
